Bonuses:
- Energy display
We defines two new classes:
1. FloatCounter (the decisions on why&how we implemented this class were explained in the Desgin Decisions
   part above).
2. NumericEnergyCounter - represents a graphical object. It receives a FloatCounter and displays its value on
   the screen.

- Background music
We added background music to the game using the soundReader in the PepseGameManager.

- Make leaf fall on click
A left click on a leaf leads to its immediate fall.
In order to implement this, we override the onMouseAction function in the Leaf class and added the needed
functionality.

- Memory game
We added the option to play a memory game in which the leaves on the trees are the game cards.
game explained:
A leaf may contain a game card image.
A right click on a leaf will cause:
If the leaf doesn't contain a game card - the leaf will perform a spin.
If the leaf does contain a game card - the game card image will get displayed.
another right click on that leaf will hide the game card and will display the default leaf renderable again
(in our case - the green block).
Only 2 game cards are allowed to be displayed In each give moment.
If the user displayed the game card on 2 leaves but they don't match (different images on the cards), both of
the game cards will get automatically turned over (=hidden).
If the user displayed the game card on 2 leaves and they do match, an animation that represents a successfull
match will get displayed (in our case - fireworks), and both of the leaves will fall off the tree, their game
card image will get deleted (they will become leaves which spins upon click), and they'll keep with their
regular life cycle.

implementation:
We created a MemoryGameCard interface which the Leaf class implements so we can treat it as a game card.
(using Polymorphism ew could address other objects in the game as game cards like terrain blocks, etc.)
We created a MemoryGameManager class which responsible for the logic of the memory game, it check when game
cards match, when they don't and there is a need to turn them over, and holds the match animation.
This class inhertis from GameObject in order to be able to display the animation on the screen.

